@main
// Code generation for the Gen1 compiler (M6b2-s3a/s3b), a subset port of
// bootstrap/crates/xuemit: MIR -> vm calls.
//
// Conventions (mirror xuemit):
// - Every local and temp lives in its own FP-relative stack slots
//   (int/bool = 1 slot; string = 3). No register allocation; V0/V1 are
//   within-instruction scratch.
// - User-function ABI: one argument register per argument (A0-A5), int/bool
//   by value; << in Ret. (Multi-slot values arrive in a later stage.)
// - println ABI: value in A0 (+len in A1 for strings), fd in A2 (1=stdout).
// - `_start` peeks C argv for `--xu`, heap-copies argv only if `args()` is
//   used (Windows always collects), then `_xu_main` and exits with main's
//   << value (0 for a void main).
//
// One deliberate difference: the Rust emitter collects the used-helper set
// during function emission; here it is computed by a pure pre-scan of the
// MIR (same set, same emission order). Drop helpers (drop_s_N / drop_a_N)
// are collected the same way and emitted after the runtime helpers.
//
// The assembler is threaded in place through `&mut Assembler`. The owning
// driver starts the chain with `mut &a`; emitters reborrow the existing
// mutable reference directly when calling helpers.

#xu/types

